{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A restart between saving gate results and completing the stage can cause delivery of an unchanged, verified commit to be refused."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A pull-request lookup failure can route delivery through a draft fallback that pushes the verified commit without applying the claimed before-any-push guard."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After an interrupted merge, an amended merge commit with preserved parents can be published without its added changes being audited or reviewed."}]}